# Weather malformed-JSON guard. Pinned to PR-1.5 (Phase 1C), which
# added an explicit DeserializationError check after deserializeJson
# in get_weather() but committed no fixture that actually exercised it.
# This scenario closes that gap.
#
# flash_seed sets location_key = BROKEN so the URL becomes
#   .../currentconditions/v1/BROKEN?apikey=TEST_KEY
# routing to test/fixtures/http/.../currentconditions/v1/BROKEN.json,
# which is intentionally truncated mid-object so ArduinoJson's
# deserializeJson returns InvalidInput / IncompleteInput. The new code
# logs "[APP] Get weather - JSON parse error: ..." and skips the
# JsonObject access; the scenario asserts no crash.
#
# The forecast endpoint deliberately has no BROKEN fixture, so it
# returns -1 (no-fixture sentinel) and exercises that branch too.

app weather
flash_seed /weather_accu.cfg "TEST_KEY\nBeijing\nBROKEN\n900000\n900000\n0\n"

wait_ms 800
assert_no_crash

action TURN_RIGHT
wait_ms 200
assert_no_crash

action RETURN
wait_ms 200
assert_no_crash
